    <briefdescription>
<para>Observed-Remove Set (OR-Set). </para>
    </briefdescription>
    <detaileddescription>
<para>Unlike 2P-Set, elements can be re-added after removal. Each add generates a unique <ref refid="structthemisdb_1_1replication_1_1crdt_1_1_dot" kindref="compound">Dot</ref>; remove operations tombstone only the specific dots observed at remove time. A concurrent add on another node will survive a concurrent remove because it carries a different dot.</para>
<para><parameterlist kind="templateparam"><parameteritem>
<parameternamelist>
<parametername>T</parametername>
</parameternamelist>
<parameterdescription>
<para>Element type (must be less-than-comparable). </para>
</parameterdescription>
</parameteritem>
</parameterlist>
</para>
    </detaileddescription>
